Package: SeMiLLa
Type: Package
Title: Drafting and Auditing Psychometric Items with Large Language Models
Version: 2.12.0
Date: 2026-10-09
Authors@R: c(
    person("Jose", "Ventura-Leon",
           email = "jventuraleon@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-2996-4244"))
    )
Description: Drafts psychometric scale items from a psychological construct
    with Large Language Models (LLMs) and audits them before any data are
    collected. It derives a working definition and dimensions from the model's
    knowledge, from user input or from 'PubMed' and 'Semantic Scholar'
    abstracts; writes items; obtains text embeddings; and checks whether items
    of the same dimension group together by ensemble clustering of those
    embeddings (semantic separability, after Voss, Wu, Javalagi and Kell
    (2026) <doi:10.1177/00131644261430762>; not factor analysis of
    responses). A pre-administration gate simulates ordinal responses under
    stated assumptions about loadings, factor correlations and social
    desirability,
    and simulated LLM judges rate content validity with Aiken's V (Aiken,
    1985 <doi:10.1177/0013164485451012>) and the score interval of Penfield
    and Giacobbi (2004) <doi:10.1207/s15327841mpee0804_3>. These checks
    describe the wording, not the behaviour of real respondents, and do not
    replace a field study.
